/P 79 0 R
/E (Measure calls to the slow verification function for 1,000 passengers and explain how condition order affects calls and audit logging.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Assume 200 passengers satisfy senior && eligible and the remaining 800 do not. With \(senior && eligible\) || verify_card\(card\), verification is called 800 times. With verify_card\(card\) || \(senior && eligible\), it is called for all 1,000 passengers. A false left operand of && skips the right side; a true left operand of || skips the right side.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (In C, && skips its right operand when its left operand is false. || skips its right operand when its left operand is true. Evaluation proceeds left to right. The operators & and | evaluate both operands and do not short-circuit. Nested if statements can express the same decision but must preserve the required verification side effects.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Short-circuit evaluation can reduce expensive calls, but mandatory audit logging takes priority. Explicitly calling verification once per passenger is the correct design when every check must be recorded.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (A railway concession is granted when the passenger is a senior citizen and the ticket class is eligible, or when a disability card is verified. Verification is a slow operation. Compare condition orders and short-circuit behaviour.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Put a cheap condition first when it is likely to decide the result and skipping the expensive check is allowed. If verification must audit every passenger, short-circuiting cannot be allowed to skip it: call verify_card explicitly once per passenger, store its result, and then evaluate the decision. For n passengers, explicit verification makes n calls; short-circuit versions make between 0 and n calls depending on data and order. Non-short-circuit & and | evaluate both operands, but use them only with valid integer/boolean operands and no unsafe side effects.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
