/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 86 0 R
/T (A while loop is appropriate because the number of months is not known in advance and the condition is checked before each month. Avoid balance != 0.0 because floating-point rounding may prevent exact equality. Stop when balance <= a small tolerance or when the balance is paid. If repayment is no greater than monthly interest, the principal does not decrease and the loan may never be repaid.)
/E (A while loop is appropriate because the number of months is not known in advance and the condition is checked before each month. Avoid balance != 0.0 because floating-point rounding may prevent exact equality. Stop when balance <= a small tolerance or when the balance is paid. If repayment is no greater than monthly interest, the principal does not decrease and the loan may never be repaid.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
