/Title (The objective is achieved: for the large prime 1,000,003, divisor tests fall from 1,000,001 to 999, a reduction of approximately 99.90%. Both algorithms use O\(1\) extra space. The original algorithm may remain acceptable for very small n because it is simpler, but the improved method is preferable for larger tickets. For many queries over a fixed range, a sieve can reduce total work further at the cost of O\(N\) memory.)
