<<
/Title (The while and carefully guarded do-while implementations perform the same checks as the for version. For n=2 or n=3, the do-while must test the bound before attempting a modulus; otherwise it may test a divisor outside the valid range. The condition i*i <= n can overflow for large values; i <= n/i avoids multiplication overflow. For an upper limit N, a Sieve of Eratosthenes takes O\(N log log N\) time and O\(N\) space, then answers each primality query in O\(1\), making it useful when many numbers up to N are queried.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 881 0 R
>>
endobj
